---
title: Pink Gin Apple Sauce
course: Side
servings: 6
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

In a #wide saucepan with a lid{} soften the @spring onions{5}(white part only, finely sliced) in the @butter{2%tbsp}, adding a little @salt{sprinkling} to prevent it scorching.

Cut the @Red Delicious apples{3} into quarters (without removing the core) and add to the pan with the onion. Pour in @gin{2%tbsp}, @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and @red chilli{1}(left whole), giving everything a good stir.

Cover the pan and cook at a medium heat until the apples are soft. This should take no more than ~{20%minutes}.

Take out the chilli pepper and then work the sauce through a #food mill or sieve{}, the skins from the apples colouring the sauce a blushing dusky pink. Stir in the remaining @gin{1%tbsp} and season to taste.